<title>USA: Dominick's declines comment on Byerly's.</title>
<headline>Dominick's declines comment on Byerly's.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHLAKE, Ill. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dominick's Supermarkets Inc on Thursday declined comment on published reports that the company planned to buy two Byerly's stores near Chicago.</p>
<p>&quot;We have no announcements and do not comment on rumors,&quot; Dominick's spokesman C. Mark Hussey told Reuters.</p>
<p>The Chicago Tribune reported on Thursday that Edina, Minnesota-based Byerly's planned to sell stores in Highland Park and Schaumburg, Illinois, to Dominick's and exit the Chicago area less than a year after its arrival.</p>
</text>
